WEBVTT

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.930
Another delicious meal, Ruriko-san!

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:08.080
Keep eating.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.480
You only get to eat this for a 
little while more, Yushi-kun.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:14.100
I guess summer vacation ends soon...

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:17.490
We'll have a big farewell party, Yushi-kun!

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:18.630
Right!

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:24.080
<i>After coming and meeting all 
the incredible people here,</i>

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.550
<i>everything I was so sure I knew fell apart.</i>

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.800
<i>It will be September soon.</i>

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.150
<i>I'll be leaving the Yokai Apartments.</i>

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:50.400
<i>For some reason, I find myself 
hoping summer never ends.</i>

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:54.540
<i>What's gotten into me? 
I'm not usually like this.</i>

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.110
Hey, Inaba! Are you here?

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:00.490
Hey! Inaba!

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:03.280
There you are.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.870
Takenaka... What are you doing here?

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:09.120
Well, you refused to invite me over.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.250
So I just came over.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.030
Th-That was because...

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:15.000
I've got my reasons!

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.190
And since I was coming...

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:22.170
I brought my friends.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.300
Takenaka, you...

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.490
Let's all have some fun!

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:05.410
<b>Fourth Haunting 
This Side</b>

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:11.280
You're playing Mahjong? Let me play.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.290
Takenaka, what are you thinking?

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:17.080
Come on, take that stick out of your ass.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:18.960
Your friend's here to hang out.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.510
Don't tell me you're gonna try and stop me.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.330
Ruriko-san, was it?

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:27.550
The chef who makes all those 
delicious-looking meals.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:30.300
I'd love it if she'd make snacks 
to go with our drinks!

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.730
Wow, this apartment is crappy.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.900
Seriously. I bet one match would 
bring the whole place down.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.600
Quiet...

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:38.970
That ain't funny.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.400
Stop it! Are you drunk?

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:47.920
You know...

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.290
You must get tired of always being a suck-up.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:52.400
A suck-up?

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:01.060
You work hard at your job and club, 
even though you don't like them.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:04.410
Well, we'll show you a good time today.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.010
So tell us how you really feel!

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:08.850
<i>How I really feel?</i>

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:12.810
<i>That's what he thought about me?</i>

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:18.070
Hey, you said you lived in the same 
building as a teenage girl, right?

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:20.280
Where are ya, girlie?

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.150
Let's drink together!

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:25.400
You're kidding me...

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:27.950
Knock it off!

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:31.900
Hey, what are you doing, suck-up?

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:36.220
Don't you know what will happen 
to you if you hurt our friend?

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.730
I know you don't like me.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:49.880
But "suck-up" or not, my livelihood's on the line.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:54.810
If nothing else, I don't have time 
to play at being thugs with you!

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:57.810
"Play"?

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:59.000
Yeah.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:01.120
Someone once told me...

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.870
It is humanity's fate to 
be drawn to outlaws...

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.590
But do you have any noble motive like that?

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:11.410
What drives you?!

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:15.090
You probably rebel against the world 
because you think it's fun or cool,

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:16.860
or something else that's easy!

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:20.080
Y-You...

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:23.990
That's what I dislike about you, Inaba!

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:28.090
You and your damned 
"I'm an adult" expression!

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:31.970
I didn't want to be an adult!

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:38.690
I'm acting like this for a goddamn reason!

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:40.210
I'm not like you!

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:43.240
What's he talking about?

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:45.340
We'll get you for that!

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:51.320
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:54.220
<i>I can't handle six of them at once!</i>

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.160
Yushi-kun, you're so cool!

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:01.530
You look cute, but you're so wild.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.720
Have fun, young people.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:07.170
Cheers!

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:10.170
<i>Those people...</i>

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:13.600
N-No!

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.520
Die, Inaba!

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.420
Shut up, brats!

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:29.060
We let you have your fun, 
and this is how you behave?

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:36.890
Wh-What?

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:38.170
Costumes?

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:41.780
You're making too much damn noise.

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:44.600
I had a really good hand, too.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.770
<i>Those tiles... Those hands.</i>

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:52.000
<i>Those are the Mahjong players?</i>

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:56.470
<i>They were oni?!</i>

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:00.730
You'd better cut this crap out, or...

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:11.810
<i>They're here.</i>

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:14.260
<i>Things you can't see.</i>

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:15.460
<i>Watching us.</i>

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:19.040
Hey, guys...

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:22.160
You understand, don't you?

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:25.610
It's best to leave Yushi-kun alone.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:29.930
There are some things in the world 
you can't get involved with.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:32.440
You're still young, right?

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:35.470
You don't want to ruin your 
whole lives, do you?

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:37.600
Do you?

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:44.500
The hell you think you're doing, 
messing up my yard?

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:50.610
And you're kids, so you don't 
get to drink and smoke!

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.490
Taste divine punishment!

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:55.310
Damn.

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:56.570
Sheesh...

00:07:56.570 --> 00:07:59.660
Fukase just wants to fight. That's all.

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:03.700
At his exhibitions, he gets 
into fights all the time.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:06.380
Some fans come to see it.

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:08.340
Sounds like pro wrestling.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.280
We'll get you for this!

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:13.000
Yeah, that's what people say when they lose.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:24.480
Hey, Yushi.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:25.890
Y-Yes?

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.270
You're more of a man now, huh?

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:35.440
Yeah.

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:46.170
<i>That night, a goodbye party was held 
for me at the Yokai Apartments.</i>

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:48.880
Now, let's eat!

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:52.070
After a fight, you want meat, beer, and food!

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:53.790
Right, here you go!

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:55.710
Meat!

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:59.200
Have some juice, Yushi-kun.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:01.280
That was really cool back there.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:03.770
M-Mariko-san!

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:04.950
Chirpity-chirp!

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:06.660
Why so embarrassed, chirp?

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:09.090
Hey, don't get the wrong idea, chirp!

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:11.830
You aren't popular with girls, chirp.

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:14.350
He isn't? Poor guy, chirp.

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:15.440
Shut up!

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:17.450
We made it in time...

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.060
Glad we turned down that overtime!

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:20.380
It smells good.

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:22.790
Thank you, thank you.

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:26.990
Here, you go.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:29.430
Excuse us.

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:32.690
Akane-sama sent us here.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:34.170
Please take this.

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.020
Akane-san?

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.170
A whole red snapper!

00:09:38.170 --> 00:09:41.390
And she said that this is for Yushi-sama.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:42.350
For me?

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:49.820
<b>"The paths we walk are not one,</b>

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:53.890
<b>but I shall not forget your face."</b>

00:09:54.710 --> 00:09:57.950
She means she won't forget you.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:01.070
Akane-san's quite the poet. 
That's an elegant poem.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:04.620
<i>Akane-san...</i>

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.700
Hey. Having fun?

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:12.900
Ryu-san!

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:14.900
Welcome back, Ryu-san!

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:17.380
I'm glad I made it in time.

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:20.250
So this is farewell, Yushi-kun?

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:22.040
Yes.

00:10:22.710 --> 00:10:26.110
How about a drink of Countess 
Bathory's blood?

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:29.220
You never change, Antiquary.

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:33.640
And I'm glad to see you don't, either, 
Blue Pearl of the Orient.

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:36.160
The beautiful Pale Blue.

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:41.420
Your hair is like that of a mermaid.

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:46.010
Would you not call me "Pale Blue"?

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:48.590
Excuse me.

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:50.550
And...

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:53.040
Don't steal my hair!

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:56.450
This hair sells for quite a bit.

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:59.480
Who said you could sell it? You—

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:01.020
It's called "Spirit Hair."

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:04.170
Hair can have spiritual powers.

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:05.050
Indeed.

00:11:05.050 --> 00:11:08.140
I put it into a crystal pendant.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:09.300
See?

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:14.860
Wives of European noblemen 
will pay any price for this.

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:24.890
A parting gift. Take it.

00:11:25.930 --> 00:11:26.700
But...

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:31.520
Thank you.

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:33.810
I'll keep it with me at all times!

00:11:33.810 --> 00:11:34.890
Yushi-kun!

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:37.190
Akine-san?

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:40.340
Then, I'll also put a prayer into it, okay?

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:51.680
Please let Yushi-kun live a normal 
life, in a normal way.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:59.610
If you leave this place, your spiritual 
abilities won't be further stimulated.

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:01.910
Don't worry, and live your life.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.450
Thanks, Akine-san.

00:12:13.970 --> 00:12:16.930
<i>Every day was like a dream.</i>

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:19.280
<i>It was strange and exciting,</i>

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:21.460
<i>and for some reason, it felt familiar.</i>

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:26.260
<i>It would be a time in my life 
I'd never forget.</i>

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:35.800
<i>And soon after, September began.</i>

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:41.280
<i>And I left this apartment building.</i>

00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:57.830
<i>Chirp, chirp, chirp!</i>

00:12:57.830 --> 00:12:59.470
<i>It's morning, chirp.</i>

00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:01.580
<i>How long are you going to sleep, chirp?</i>

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.930
<i>Hey, Yushi, chirp!</i>

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:08.430
<i>You guys again?</i>

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:16.510
<i>I see.</i>

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:18.540
<i>Of course they aren't here.</i>

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:28.730
<i>At the second term's start, I moved 
into the new student dorm.</i>

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:31.050
It's amazing!

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:33.280
Everything is so shiny and new!

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:36.320
Feels like we're kinda lucky, huh?

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:40.070
I heard the old dorm was thirty years old.

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:43.510
If you're paying the same, wouldn't you 
rather live in a new place?

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:49.360
<i>This is Hiroyuki Ishii, a first-year 
and one of my roommates.</i>

00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:54.440
Supposedly, the food around 
here is good, too.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:56.580
That sounds great.

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:03.020
Sorry for being noisy.

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:12.730
<i>Keisuke Kaga, a second-year 
and another roommate,</i>

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:15.070
<i>was quiet and hard to talk to.</i>

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:20.040
<i>But better than thinking 
he's older and superior.</i>

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.350
Let's go eat.

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:24.300
Y-Yeah.

00:14:27.820 --> 00:14:31.640
<i>I thought that since there wasn't any 
adult supervision at a student dorm,</i>

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:34.240
<i>nasty bullying and stuff would be common.</i>

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:38.060
<i>But evidently, there are more 
and more people like Kaga...</i>

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:41.780
I'm gonna hit the restroom.

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:43.310
I'll see you there.

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:56.540
Lost? What's your room number?

00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.390
304.

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:01.040
Thanks.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:04.170
<i>People won't bully you, 
but they won't help you.</i>

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:07.750
<i>My relationships are 
becoming more superficial.</i>

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:12.330
Wow, this is as good as they said!

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:14.840
It's also included in the rent, 
and it's plenty, right?

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:16.900
Y-Yeah...

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:21.660
<i>I do think it's good.</i>

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:26.430
<i>But why does it seem like it isn't 
nearly as good as Ruriko-san's?</i>

00:15:27.910 --> 00:15:32.380
<i>Ruriruri's dream was to 
have a little restaurant.</i>

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:37.500
She died before she could, so she's 
probably still attached to the idea.

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:40.090
A restaurant?

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:42.290
She'd quit her hostess job

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:45.250
and was ready to run her 
own restaurant, when...

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:52.750
She was killed by a customer who'd 
stalked her since her hostess days.

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:55.400
And her body was sliced into pieces,

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:57.950
most of which weren't found.

00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:01.040
Ruriruri died before fulfilling her dream,

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:04.630
and the last thing she saw was her own hands.

00:16:08.220 --> 00:16:09.990
I see...

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:21.960
<b>My dream came true, 
and now I'm very happy.</b>

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:22.680
"My dream came true, and now I'm very happy."

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:26.600
<i>That's why.</i>

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:29.800
<i>Ruriko-san's food was made with love.</i>

00:16:30.810 --> 00:16:34.910
<i>She wanted those who ate her 
food to think it was delicious.</i>

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:39.090
<i>That pure desire made her every 
dish into a sign of her love.</i>

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:40.900
<i>But...</i>

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:43.390
I gave you extra rice!

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:54.820
<i>There's no way to put love into that.</i>

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:06.510
<i>It's like when I lived with my uncle.</i>

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:11.230
<i>It feels... suffocating.</i>

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:15.980
Takenaka?

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:18.990
What happened to your face?

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:20.660
Were you hit?

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:23.070
It isn't your problem, suck-up!

00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:28.500
Takenaka...

00:17:49.540 --> 00:17:53.800
Um, Kaga-san, can I talk to you?

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:57.130
It's about one of my classmates.

00:18:07.090 --> 00:18:11.070
<i>Even still, my school life 
continued without a hitch.</i>

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:15.870
<i>A so-called normal life, with no problems.</i>

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:21.280
<i>But was this what I really wanted?</i>

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:23.330
<i>Was this...</i>

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:28.030
What? What's going on?

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:32.120
The cops caught some drug dealers.

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:34.830
Let me go! I don't know anything!

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:37.700
That's...

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:39.870
Wasn't one of them a high schooler?

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:41.180
Seriously?

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:43.240
What an idiot...

00:18:43.550 --> 00:18:44.860
<i>Takenaka!</i>

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:55.440
<b>Joutou Business High School</b>

00:18:50.890 --> 00:18:55.440
I did hear rumors that he'd gotten 
involved with a bad crowd...

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:58.310
I saw them hanging out near the station.

00:18:58.310 --> 00:18:59.270
Me, too.

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:01.570
I knew they were dangerous.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:04.770
He was a normal guy from 
a normal family, right?

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:09.120
Those are the guys who go crazy, sometimes.

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:13.730
<i>If I'd listened to him more,</i>

00:19:14.050 --> 00:19:16.050
<i>would things have turned out differently?</i>

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:24.960
<i>He might have thought 
that I'd understand him.</i>

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:29.390
<i>That we were both people who 
couldn't get along with the rest.</i>

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:32.680
So tell us how you really feel!

00:19:33.240 --> 00:19:34.010
<i>But...</i>

00:19:37.490 --> 00:19:40.520
You and your damned 
"I'm an adult" expression!

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:43.570
It isn't your problem, suck-up!

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:48.700
<i>But I let go of his hand.</i>

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:53.850
<i>I couldn't understand him.</i>

00:19:54.430 --> 00:19:57.800
<i>I thought that he and I had different 
reasons for being alone.</i>

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:02.840
<i>I didn't want him comparing my 
fears and complaints to his.</i>

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:27.450
Not today, either?

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:15.160
<i>I just wanted to talk. 
I wanted to see everyone.</i>

00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:18.370
<i>For the first time in a while, I returned 
to the Yokai Apartments.</i>

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:23.880
<i>But...</i>

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:27.570
<i>I'm...</i>

00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:35.380
<i>I'm on this side now, aren't I?</i>

00:23:10.360 --> 00:23:15.710
Will I end up forgetting my dreamlike
days at the Yokai Apartments someday?

00:23:15.710 --> 00:23:18.310
Oh, come on. Have some food and cheer up.

00:23:18.310 --> 00:23:20.550
You're... Wait, who are you again?

00:23:20.550 --> 00:23:22.550
I'm Sato! Sato!

00:23:22.550 --> 00:23:24.710
I'm not going to treat you,
if you say things like that.

00:23:24.710 --> 00:23:26.280
I remember now!

00:23:27.240 --> 00:23:30.150
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:29.840 --> 00:23:32.050
<b>Fifth Haunting
A Place to Call Home</b>

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:31.710
A Place to Call Home.

00:23:32.040 --> 00:23:34.930
Sato-san! This oden is so good!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:35.750
Right?
